    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0591" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg497"/>

                <head>No. 327.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-24"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 24, 1886</date>.
                        (Received December 27.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d327-f1"/> of the 11th ultimo, I have the honor to inform you that I
                    am requested by the Earl of Iddesleigh to acquaint you that Her Majesty’s
                    Government have desired the Canadian Government to furnish them with a report on
                    the circumstances attending the alleged inhospitable treatment of United States
                    fishing schooners <hi rendition="#italic">Laura Say ward</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jennie Seavers</hi> by the Canadian authorities.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
